From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:11:05 -0700
Subject: GL: Reset base level before TexStorage2D on PowerVR GPUs

PowerVR GPUs have a driver bug when glTexStorage2D is called
on a texture with a non-zero base level already applied.
This workaround resets the base level to zero before making
the TexStorage2D call, and restores the base level to its
original level afterwards.

Bug: chromium:551573368
Change-Id: I334f242842f01bdd10fc65200f81ff3b65867bec
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8283072
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>

